<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Rallybit release notes and product changes."><title>Changelog — Rallybit</title><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css?v=6.2"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any"><link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/assets/brand/rallybit-icon-32.png"><link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="192x192" href="/assets/brand/rallybit-icon-192.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/brand/apple-touch-icon.png"></head><body><div id="header-placeholder"></div><main><section class="content-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Release notes</span><h1>Rallybit changelog</h1><p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:650px;margin:auto">Major improvements, fixes, and product decisions in one clear timeline.</p></div></section><section class="content-wrap"><article><span class="eyebrow">Version 7.2.1 · 19 July 2026</span><h2>Restart-safe interactive sessions</h2><p>Live activity checks, quizzes, and community pulses now recover from bot or Raspberry Pi restarts without losing their timer or recorded participation.</p><h3>What changed</h3><ul><li>Added durable ledgers for active quizzes and community pulses.</li><li>Activity checks now preserve a settings snapshot and use idempotent participant awards.</li><li>Quiz answers, pulse responses, buttons, and remaining timers are restored at startup.</li><li>Expired sessions finish automatically after recovery.</li><li>Session restoration runs before recurring schedulers to prevent duplicate automatic posts.</li></ul></article><article><span class="eyebrow">Version 7.2.0 · 19 July 2026</span><h2>Configurable security suite</h2><p>Rallybit now includes per-server security commands without importing the unrelated ticketing or destructive server-setup systems from the reference bot.</p><h3>What changed</h3><ul><li>Added a top-level scam-detection honeypot with immediate ban or kick actions.</li><li>Added a configurable Discord account-age gate with DM and appeal settings.</li><li>Added anti-bot, anti-webhook, anti-integration, dangerous-permission, anti-nuke, anti-spam, and optional automod modules.</li><li>Added trusted roles, security logs, owner alerts, persistent history, quarantine, lockdown, panic mode, invite purge, and security audits.</li><li>All automatic modules are disabled until configured by each server.</li></ul></article><article><span class="eyebrow">Version 7.1.2 · 19 July 2026</span><h2>Community revive role notifications</h2><p>Quiz rounds, anonymous pulses, and staff-triggered icebreakers can now notify a chosen server role without exposing the server to broad or accidental mentions.</p><h3>What changed</h3><ul><li>Added an optional role to automatic quiz schedules and manual quiz rounds.</li><li>Added <code>/community pingrole</code> and <code>/community settings</code>.</li><li>Community pulses notify the configured role by default and support a silent option.</li><li>Staff can choose whether an icebreaker should notify the role.</li><li>Rallybit permits only the selected role and never falls back to <code>@everyone</code>.</li></ul></article>
<article><span class="eyebrow">Version 7.1.1 · 19 July 2026</span><h2>Automatic quiz role pings</h2><p>Recurring quizzes can now notify an optional server role, such as a Chat Revive role, when a round begins.</p><h3>What changed</h3><ul><li>Added an optional role selector to <code>/quiz setup</code>.</li><li>Added <code>/quiz pingrole</code> for changing or disabling the ping without rebuilding the schedule.</li><li>Added safe mention handling so Rallybit never falls back to <code>@everyone</code>.</li><li>Automatic quizzes still run if a configured role is deleted or can no longer be mentioned.</li></ul></article>
<article><span class="eyebrow">Version 7.1 · 19 July 2026</span><h2>Community Play & Moderation</h2><p>Rallybit now supports recurring community quizzes, anonymous pulse checks, conversation starters, and a complete interactive moderation workflow.</p><h3>What changed</h3><ul><li>Added manual and scheduled random quizzes with category selection, hidden answers, speed bonuses, explanations, streaks, and server quiz rankings.</li><li>Added an interactive member moderation panel with warnings, warning removal, history, timeouts, timeout removal, kicks, bans, message clearing, nickname changes, and role controls.</li><li>Added permission and role-hierarchy checks to every moderation action.</li><li>Added anonymous community pulse checks with aggregate-only completed history.</li><li>Added casual, gaming, creative, and debate icebreakers.</li><li>Updated the website, command centre, setup guide, feature guide, and invite permissions.</li></ul></article>
<article><span class="eyebrow">Version 7.0 · 18 July 2026</span><h2>Rallybit begins</h2><p>Activity Check was rebuilt and renamed Rallybit with a more original interface, a clearer product structure, and a completely refreshed dashboard.</p><h3>What changed</h3><ul><li>Introduced the Rallybit brand across the website, dashboard, bot, and documentation.</li><li>Made automation, detailed logs, custom buttons, longer checks, analytics, and complete configuration available to every server.</li><li>Removed the old feature tiers, access gates, and fragmented entitlement systems.</li><li>Rebuilt Discord sign-in with OAuth state verification and safer session handling.</li><li>Moved credentials out of source files and into environment configuration.</li><li>Replaced fragmented legacy admin tools with one restricted developer panel.</li><li>Improved responsive layouts across desktop, tablet, and mobile.</li></ul></article>
</section></main><div id="footer-placeholder"></div><script src="/script.js?v=5.0"></script></body></html>
